          "git_sha": "881a342d5daf0c02f938a5d3dfb56e8098791709",
          "line_end": 61,
          "line_start": 48,
          "path": "SECURITY.md",
          "repository": "alexgreensh/outsourcerer",
          "url": "https://github.com/alexgreensh/outsourcerer/blob/0ad71828e1188dc5c90e1bbde57d28a748d76d0b/SECURITY.md#L48-L61"
        },
        {
          "commit": "0ad71828e1188dc5c90e1bbde57d28a748d76d0b",
          "git_sha": "c3b4dbdec07c22f27ffcc9f185d8996405548535",
          "line_end": 270,
          "line_start": 266,
          "path": "README.md",
          "repository": "alexgreensh/outsourcerer",
          "url": "https://github.com/alexgreensh/outsourcerer/blob/0ad71828e1188dc5c90e1bbde57d28a748d76d0b/README.md#L266-L270"
        }
      ],
      "review_state": "mechanically_checked",
      "slice_ids": [
        "slc_c6ffa549190b94ddacf246e23aa79aafa169f6c8293ba99a80f7f123667a429a",
        "slc_e63019277956650b01c92153b9b103ddbb2754d477629ff00ce33fa9ae74e938"
      ],
      "text": "Before any cloud delegation, a hard-block refuses the route if credential files (.env, id_rsa, credentials, etc.) exist anywhere in the working tree; the scan runs on every call and fails closed."
    },
    {
      "basis": "documented",
      "claim_id": "clm_a8ac17ae18bb73c54e70b647c6c55e45617787687a898ab2ae07ec5193c8b0c7",
      "evidence_type": "organizational_statement",
      "facet": "tools-permissions",
      "kind": "observation",
      "locators": [
        {
          "commit": "0ad71828e1188dc5c90e1bbde57d28a748d76d0b",
          "git_sha": "881a342d5daf0c02f938a5d3dfb56e8098791709",
          "line_end": 41,
          "line_start": 34,
          "path": "SECURITY.md",
          "repository": "alexgreensh/outsourcerer",
          "url": "https://github.com/alexgreensh/outsourcerer/blob/0ad71828e1188dc5c90e1bbde57d28a748d76d0b/SECURITY.md#L34-L41"
        }
      ],
      "review_state": "mechanically_checked",
      "slice_ids": [
        "slc_869b26dd087feeee260aa4f4c6f3ed06bff7b21dc786259cb5c8fd2515f00eec"
      ],
      "text": "Keys are read one variable at a time from ~/.env via targeted grep, never sourcing the whole file, and keys are never written into command-line arguments, logs, or config."
    },
